<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Xizong of Tang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">862–888</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Li Xuan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Xizong of Tang, personal name Li Xuan, reigned from 873 to 888. Raised to the throne as a boy, he left government to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tian">Tian</a> Lingzi while the rebellions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-xianzhi">Wang Xianzhi</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huang-chao">Huang Chao</a> spread, and when Huang Chao took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a> in 881 he fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chengdu">Chengdu</a>. He returned in 885 after the rebellion was crushed, but real power had passed to regional military governors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-xizong-of-tang.jpg" alt="Emperor Xizong of Tang" width="320" height="490" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%94%90%E5%83%96%E5%AE%97%E5%B8%9D%EF%BC%88%E6%AE%98%E5%94%90%E4%BA%94%E4%BB%A3%E5%8F%B2%E6%BC%94%E7%BE%A9%E5%82%B3%EF%BC%89.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
